It was my birthday, so I felt lucky and started a game as Samurai on a
friends nethack server (so we have all our friends bones and nothing
else) and went down a few levels. Found a big potions shop, which I
resolved to rob. Then, next level down, I found a pretty big general
store with a few rather nice items, namely Sunsword! I resolved to rob
that even sooner.

Went down a few more levels when, horror of horrors, I bet a nymph and,
in my infinite impatience, she robbed by of everything but my wakizashi
and an oilskin cloak. No biggy, I thought, I'll just kill her slowly
and carefully.

I stalked her into a room, threw my wakizashi at her and then I
remembered. I'd had a wand of digging. Oh dear. She used it and dug
down. Great.

I leapt after her, with all the fearless rage of someone who's hated
nymphs since the very dawn of time. I chased around the level which was
thankfully sparse on monsters willing to exploit my AC:10.

The level I was on was the Oracle level, but I had no time for chatting
to her, I had a nymph to kill. Stepping around a black unicorn, I found
her asleep next to a statue. I gave her a good poking, but she woke and
ran off.

I found a spear on the floor, which would come in handy. Then, I hear a
noise. Then I heard something crashing through the floor. Oh dear, oh
dear.

So, with a grimace (and not a little profanity on IRC) I looked for the
room she'd dug down in. I stumbled across it but, alas, before leaping
down the hole, I fell into another trap. A pit of spikes. Poisoned
spikes.

With my strength now a paltry 11, I pulled myself out of the pit and
leapt down the hole after her. Looking around this new level, I saw a
chest which turned out to contain an egg.

Another useful weapon! Just as I was about to go and find the bitch who
ruined my life, she wandered into the room casually. I can just imagine
her smoking a cigarette and saying, "Hey."

Livid with rage, I threw my egg, then my spear, circling around,
picking it up and throwing it at her again, desperately trying to kill
her before she digs down. She dug down. Oh dear, oh dear, oh dear.

I grab my spear and, quite possibly screaming, jumped down the hole
she'd made to end her. The room I'm in is empty, so I walk around. In
the next room, a carniverous ape runs at me. I decide to take him in,
ending up having to #pray so I can survive and kill him. Picking up my
spear, a woodland elf strolls into the room. With very little HP, I
decide to leg it for some stairs.

In the room with stairs, I see a potion, which, in desperation, I
quaff. It's a potion of levitation. Rather luckily, I found some up
stairs before the elf found me, so I floated up them into an empty
room. I decide to wait, healing and getting rid of my levitation before
venturing back down.

Now, at this point, a little interlude is necessary. A long time ago on
this server, I once, as a lawful Samurai, sacrificed a wererat at an
altar. I forget they counted as human and, after I was destroyed by the
major demon Yeenoghu for my sins. I hoped I hadn't left a bones then.
Backstory over.

So there I am, waiting in a room with only a little sword for company,
bouncing gently off the ceiling, cursing the bitch who did this to me,
cursing everything ever related to nethack. I looked at my strength and
wept, for it was 11. I looked at my HP and wept, because it was only a
few points above 11.

I sat alone in this room, waiting, healing and crying when...
suddenly... I was no longer alone. A lovely bright pink & is stood
right next to me.

Oh dear.
Oh dear.
Oh dear.
Oh dear.

Yeenoghu gives me a big, big smile. I look nervously back. It's all
over. It has to be.

I take a step away and he magic missiles me. That's it. It's all over.
It has to be.

I survive with 1HP, make it out the door and down a corridor, I thought
I'd lost him. Yeenoghu teleported right next to me, no doubt still
beaming.

As he clubs me to death with his flail, I have a fleeting vision of the
nymph hiring the major demon to come and hunt me down in exchange for
the gold that BITCH stole from me. With the contract carried out,
Yeenoghu returned to his bed and the nymph and the RNG ran off happily,
hand in hand, singing and skipping down the road.


